                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sarcasm",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "345cf3da-79c3-38cb-b865-835ee839ffa2",
                                        "entry_id": "0236e9fd-fa86-39fe-8d00-ec55fc37b896",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Use of acerbic language to mock or convey contempt, often using verbal irony and (in speech) often marked by overemphasis and sneering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a63e8371-c776-4fd3-baf6-0886b24b1461",
                                                "sense_id": "345cf3da-79c3-38cb-b865-835ee839ffa2",
                                                "text": "Although the Celebrity was almost impervious to sarcasm, he was now beginning to exhibit visible signs of uneasiness, the consciousness dawning upon him that his eccentricity was not receiving the ovation it merited."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "321904ff-b632-42dc-a4d4-a9992f434ca2",
                                                "sense_id": "345cf3da-79c3-38cb-b865-835ee839ffa2",
                                                "text": "2015, Alex Kozinski, Demuth v. County of Los Angeles, 798 F.3d 837, 839 (9th Cir. 2015).\nWhile challenging someone equipped with a badge, handcuffs and a gun to “arrest me” was unwise on Demuth’s part, we fail to see what legal difference her statement makes. Demuth certainly could not authorize her own arrest and, in any event, Li could not reasonably have believed that Demuth was volunteering for handcuffs. Demuth was obviously employing “a literary device known as sarcasm.” [Citation omitted.] Her statement was a snide way of refusing; no reasonable officer could have thought otherwise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14a81f70-7beb-3c33-a60f-f9113e053c0d",
                                        "entry_id": "0236e9fd-fa86-39fe-8d00-ec55fc37b896",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An individual act of the above."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ebbd0b6f-d80b-4c8c-ab99-020d20b973cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "ccd97fb7-6c12-3314-983f-b5e098007979",
                        "source_sense_id": "71231e35-89aa-3283-973c-6ffb769196ae",
                        "source_sense_description": "de mate waarin men beledigend en honend is",
                        "target_lang_word": "scorn",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scorn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8cdea1e-da1d-3502-a6b1-5bd831e7600d",
                                        "entry_id": "bd844b3a-eacd-3015-9db9-5dffa32cebdb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To feel or display contempt or disdain for something or somebody; to despise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a083eb3-7272-42da-a92a-adb72d14ee3f",
                                                "sense_id": "b8cdea1e-da1d-3502-a6b1-5bd831e7600d",
                                                "text": "The Cry is ſtill, they come: our Caſtles ſtrength / Will laugh a Siedge to ſcorne"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b29daf2-ea84-4474-be63-067730f7cf8e",
                                                "sense_id": "b8cdea1e-da1d-3502-a6b1-5bd831e7600d",
                                                "text": "We scorn what is in itself contemptible or disgraceful."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c69ea51-8f3c-33aa-b457-6de0003037fc",
                                        "entry_id": "bd844b3a-eacd-3015-9db9-5dffa32cebdb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To reject, turn down."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45933f4c-e43d-4088-93b8-68f00ccd5cea",
                                                "sense_id": "1c69ea51-8f3c-33aa-b457-6de0003037fc",
                                                "text": "He scorned her romantic advances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e10097e-d484-4a9d-b0e2-0a916af0e2d2",
                                                "sense_id": "1c69ea51-8f3c-33aa-b457-6de0003037fc",
                                                "text": "Heav'n has no Rage, like Love to Hatred turn'd, / Nor Hell a Fury, like a Woman ſcorn'd."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5e83942-2a26-3ed0-bc8c-20cff18a1827",
                                        "entry_id": "bd844b3a-eacd-3015-9db9-5dffa32cebdb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To refuse to do something, as beneath oneself."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f97fe74e-ad65-418a-b024-54f6d3309ea3",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e83942-2a26-3ed0-bc8c-20cff18a1827",
                                                "text": "She scorned to show weakness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "055624d4-d2ac-3414-a857-2edad5c02a51",
                                        "entry_id": "bd844b3a-eacd-3015-9db9-5dffa32cebdb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To scoff, to express contempt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32842f26-56ed-42ca-9565-9417f009fde2",
                                                "sense_id": "055624d4-d2ac-3414-a857-2edad5c02a51",
                                                "text": "For miſerie doth braueſt mindes abate, / And make them ſeeke for that they wont to ſcorne, / Of fortune and of hope at once forlorne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scorn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fd0a426-2245-369f-821a-d29acf87f457",
                                        "entry_id": "9e5d1e2d-b955-3239-b60c-812004a5ab03",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Contempt or disdain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19772da6-9fcf-4831-97db-03a4051f160b",
                                                "sense_id": "7fd0a426-2245-369f-821a-d29acf87f457",
                                                "text": "Rain of tears, real, mist of imagined scorn"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a874670-fa93-3808-b827-c019f6c3753d",
                                        "entry_id": "9e5d1e2d-b955-3239-b60c-812004a5ab03",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A display of disdain; a slight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42334e8c-ef65-4097-80b2-2e80e5ce2358",
                                                "sense_id": "2a874670-fa93-3808-b827-c019f6c3753d",
                                                "text": "VVith ſcoffes and ſcornes, and contumelious taunts, / In open Market-place produc't they me, / To be a publique ſpectacle to all: / Here, ſayd they, is the Terror of the French, / The Scar-Crovv that affrights our Children ſo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79842229-e5d4-4873-808a-1260348fe65b",
                                                "sense_id": "2a874670-fa93-3808-b827-c019f6c3753d",
                                                "text": "Every sullen frown and bitter scorn / But fanned the fuel that too fast did burn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4c54ce9-60e0-3dc7-b240-d3064d840fdf",
                                        "entry_id": "9e5d1e2d-b955-3239-b60c-812004a5ab03",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object of disdain, contempt, or derision."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cadcda1-71fe-40f2-9407-4db683e5a9c9",
                                                "sense_id": "f4c54ce9-60e0-3dc7-b240-d3064d840fdf",
                                                "text": "Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and a derision to them that are round about us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
